# Error handling

Throw typed errors from services. Map them in Yoga. Never send stack traces, Prisma messages, or secrets to the client.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
catch (e) { return { message: String(e) } } // leaks internals
catch (e) {}                                // swallows failures

// ✅ GOOD
throw new NotFoundError("Lead not found")
throw new BusinessRuleError("BidRequest is closed")
throw new ConflictError("This BidRequest already has a winner")
```

Types: `AuthenticationError`, `AuthorizationError`, `ValidationError` (Zod issues), `NotFoundError`, `ConflictError`, `BusinessRuleError`, `InternalServerError`.

Client-safe payload: `{ code, message, fields? }`. Log the real error server-side with requestId.

## Logging

Structured JSON: `requestId`, `userId`, `organizationId`, `operation`, `entityType`, `entityId`, `durationMs`, `error`.

Never log: passwords, hashes, session tokens, `AUTH_SECRET`, Stripe secrets, R2 keys, Resend keys, raw card data, webhook signing payloads beyond event id.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
logger.info("stripe", { secret: process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, body })

// ✅ GOOD
logger.info("stripe.webhook", { eventId, type, organizationId })
```

Audit payloads follow the same redaction. Prefer `ConflictError` for unique-constraint races (second bid accept).
